# Probe reports written while working on the neovim plugin. Every file here deploys
# to the home directory unless it is named, and a report is not configuration.
#
# Unanchored, unlike the same two patterns in .gitignore. chezmoi rejects the
# whole source state on a leading slash here -- every command then fails rather
# than ignoring one file -- so the two files spell these differently on purpose.
p0*.txt
# nvim writes its log to ~/.local/state/nvim/nvim.log, and falls back to
# nvim.log in the working directory when it cannot write there. A log is not
# configuration, and this name does not begin with a dot, so chezmoi would
# deploy it.
nvim.log
